{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Mercury Retrograde", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Lost File", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 17, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Exchange information about hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Narrative Tenses: Simple Past and Past Continuous", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Narrative tenses are verb tenses that are used to talk about the past. They are often found in stories and descriptions of past events, such as personal anecdotes.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> has several uses in a narrative.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol> <li>To talk about habits in the past: What did the character routinely do? Use adverbs of frequency to add detail here. </li>For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Henry <span class=\"strong\">always made</span> others laugh.</span><br/> <br/> <li>To talk about duration in the past: How long did something happen? Use the prepositions for.</li>For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Henry <span class=\"strong\">lived</span> there <span class=\"strong\">for 5 years</span>.</span><br/> <br/> <li>Completed actions: What was the sequence of events and how did they come to an end?</li> For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Henry, badly frightened, <span class=\"strong\">threw </span>open the trap door in the floor and <span class=\"strong\">climbed </span>down the ladder into the small, dark hole.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">Past Continuous</span> is useful in a narrative. Here are some uses:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol> <li>To talk about an interrupted action: you use the Past Continuous as background to a more important or dramatic event, which is in the past. </li>For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Henry <span class=\"strong\">was preparing</span> dinner when he sliced his finger.</span><br/> <br/> <li>To talk about a simultaneous action. You use the continuous tense to demonstrate that the two actions are happening at the same time, not one after the other.</li>For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">was saving</span> the document to my hard drive regularly and <span class=\"strong\">backing up</span> my files to an external hard drive too. But somehow I deleted this document. </span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I was working on a file that was saved on my desktop.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Suddenly, it disappeared! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Somehow I deleted this document.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I unplugged the modem and plugged it back in.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Relative Clause or Noun Clause?", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "After nouns, you use <span class=\"italic\"> that </span> to introduce both relative and noun clauses. <br/> Let's look at  important differences between the two.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">She made a promise <span class=\"strong\">that she would return all the money</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In this example, the <span class=\"underline\">noun clause</span> (<span class=\"strong\">that she would return all the money</span>) adds meaning to the word <span class=\"italic\">promise </span>and tells us what it is. You cannot replace <span class=\"italic\">that </span>with <span class=\"italic\">which</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">She made a promise <span class=\"strong\">that she failed to keep</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In this example, we don't know what the promise was (there is no added meaning). You can replace <span class=\"italic\">that </span>with <span class=\"italic\">which </span>in <span class=\"underline\">relative clauses</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at some more examples from the text. Can you identify whether they use noun clauses or relative clauses? ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I found all the other files that I had saved.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I tend to follow the superstitions that are just common sense, like \u201cdon't walk under a ladder\u201d.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I swear that there's something really strange going on.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Are you sure it's not just a coincidence that they are both having problems at the same time?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I really believe that there's more to it than just a coincidence.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do you believe that some of our actions can bring us bad luck?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "desktop", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the \u200bscreen \u200barea of a \u200bpersonal \u200bcomputer when no \u200bprograms are being used", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was working on a file that was saved on my desktop.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about strange events and technology.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "at my wit's end", "type": "name"}, {"content": "perplexed; at the end of one's ideas ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm at my wit's end! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "coincidence", "type": "name"}, {"content": "when two or more things unexpectedly happen at the same time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are you sure it's not just a coincidence that they are both having problems at the same time?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to spill", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cause or allow something to flow over the edge of its container, especially unintentionally", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Although, I do throw salt over my shoulder if I spill it on the table and I don't open my umbrella inside.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "common sense", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the \u200bability to use good \u200bjudgment in making \u200bdecisions and to \u200blive in a \u200breasonable and \u200bsafe way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I tend to follow the superstitions that are just common sense, like \u201cdon't walk under a ladder\u201d. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "external", "type": "name"}, {"content": "happening \u200boutside; from an outside source", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was saving the document to my hard drive regularly and backing up my files to an external hard drive too.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hard drive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200bdisk on which a large \u200bamount of \u200binformation can be \u200bstored and used by a \u200bcomputer or other \u200bpiece of \u200belectronic \u200bequipment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think that my hard drive may be corrupt.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to delete", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to remove all or part of an electronic or written text", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Somehow I deleted this document.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "On the Internet, research superstitions in your country or another country.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose one superstition that is interesting to you and do more research.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a paragraph about the superstition that you chose. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your paragraph to your group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to the other students read their paragraphs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In your group, decide which superstition is the most believable and which is the least believable.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research a superstition on the Internet.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a paragraph about a superstition.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my paragraph to a group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I listen to other paragraphs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I choose the most and least believable superstition.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can discuss coincidences and strange events.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can say what happened and what was happening.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express opinions, beliefs, events or situations.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What kinds of superstitions have you heard of?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Do you believe that any superstitions are true? Which ones?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Has something ever happened to you that you couldn't explain?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_na